th persistent sojourn‐time expectation: Analysis and synthesis\n\nInternational Journal of Robust and Nonlinear Control\n\n  * August 2023\n  * 33(17):10764-10781\n\nDOI:10.1002/rnc.6912\n\nAuthors:\n\nKaixin Xu\n\nKaixin Xu\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nBo Cai\n\nBo Cai\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nShengao Lu\n\nShengao Lu\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nYe Liang\n\n  * Harbin Institute of Technology\n\nShow all 5 authors Hide\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\n## Abstract and Figures\n\nThis paper is concerned with the problems of stability and stabilization for discrete‐time switched linear systems with a new class of switching signals. The considered switching signals are of random mode‐dependent sojourn‐time (RMST) property, which is capable of describing the mode‐dependent sojourn‐time period consisting of a fixed part with no switching and a random part with known sojourn‐time expectation. \nDOI: 10.1002/rnc.6912\n\n\nAbstract\n\nThis paper is concerned with the problems of stability and stabilization for\n\ndiscrete-time switched linear systems with a new class of switching signals.\n\nThe considered switching signals are of random mode-dependent sojourn-time\n\n(RMST) property, which is capable of describing the mode-dependent\n\nsojourn-time period consisting of a fixed part with no switching and a random\n\npart with known sojourn-time expectation. Compared with the previous studies\n\nassuming that the switching dynamics of the random part can be described by a\n\nMarkov chain, the length of the random part is allowed to obey any distribution\n\nincluding geometric distribution. Besides, the mode switching of RMST switch-\n\ning is arbitrary indicating that it requires no statistical information of transition\n\nprobabilities. The criteria of stability and stabilization are derived for the RMST\n\nswitchedsystems.TofurtherreducethelimitationofRMSTswitchingonswitch-\n\ning frequency, a concept of random mode-dependent persistent sojourn-time\n\n(RMPST)isproposed. Then, in the presence of asynchronousswitching,the con-\n\nditions of the existence of controllers are presented for the switched systems\n\nwith persistent sojourn-time expectation. A numerical example and a practical\n\nexample of a space robot manipulator are given to demonstrate the effectiveness\n\nand applicability of the developed theoretical results.\n\nKEYWORDS\n\nasynchronous switching, random switching, sojourn-time, stabilizing control, switched systems\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nACTA ARITHMETICA (https://www.impan.pl/shop/publication/transaction/download/product/83041)\nciteturn1search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; 20736 log(12) ... 18 ... 130321 log(19) ... σ ∈A(τ) for bases 4 ≤b ≤23.\n416\nH. Faure et al.\nTable 1. Numerical results for the full search in A(τ)\nb\nΦσ,(2)\nb\n−(Φσ\nb )2\nlog b\nnum. value\nσ\n2\n5\n192 log(2)\n0.037570\nid\n3\n4\n81 log(3)\n0.044950\nid\n4\n5\n96 log(4)\n0.037570\n(2, 1)\n5\n112\n1875 log(5)\n0.037114\n(3, 1)\n6\n343\n5184 log(6)\n0.036927\n(4, 1)\n7\n512\n7203 log(7)\n0.036529\n(2, 0)(5, 1)(6, 4)\n8\n5\n64 log(8)\n0.037570\n(4, 1)(6, 3)\n9\n512\n6561 log(9)\n0.035516\n(5, 1)(7, 3)\n10\n3391\n40000 log(10)\n0.036817\n(2, 8, 4, 6, 9, 7, 1, 5, 3, 0)\n11\n3680\n43923 log(11)\n0.034940\n(7, 1)(4, 2)(9, 3)(8, 6)\n12\n1759\n20736 log(12)\n0.034137\n(5, 4, 10, 6, 7, 1)(8, 9, 3, 2)\n13\n574\n6591 log(13)\n0.033953\n(5, 12, 7, 0)(10, 11, 2, 1)(8, 9, 4, 3)\n14\n41581\n460992 log(14)\n0.034178\n(2, 5, 7, 3, 12, 4, 0)(9, 13, 11, 8, 6, 10, 1)\n15\n4714\n50625 log(15)\n0.034385\n(8, 10, 12, 9, 1)(5, 13, 6, 4, 2)(11, 3)\n16\n17573\n196608 log(16)\n0.032237\n(7, 6, 14, 8, 9, 1)(12, 11, 5, 2)(4, 10, 13, 3)\n17\n8040\n83521 log(17)\n0.033977\n